rem RSA Encryption
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=182
rem Sum the exponents e coprime to
rem (p - 1) (q - 1) that leave the
rem fewest messages unconcealed

use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

option P integer = 1009
option Q integer = 3643

rem m^e = m mod p q has 1 + gcd(e - 1,
rem p - 1) solutions mod p and likewise
rem mod q. Their product counts the
rem unconcealed messages.
Phi = (P - 1) * (Q - 1)
E = 2 to Phi - 1 array
Coprime = (E Phi gcd) equal 1
Prev = E - 1
Gp = Prev (P - 1) gcd
Gq = Prev (Q - 1) gcd
Fixed = (1 + Gp) * (1 + Gq)
Cand = Fixed filter Coprime array
Least = Cand min
Best = Fixed equal Least
Pick = E filter (Coprime and Best) array
Answer = Pick sum
Answer print
